Fluence Presentation Planning Document (Draft)

Goal
Present Fluence as a functional, scalable system that combines:
- real-world data
- backend architecture
- AI-driven insights
without locking into rigid claims

--------------------------------------------------

Overall Flow (High-Level)

1. Problem → Why this matters
2. What Fluence is (concept + vision)
3. System overview (high-level)
4. Key features
5. AI component (flexible depth)
6. Demo
7. Challenges + future direction

--------------------------------------------------

Section Ideas

1. Introduction / Motivation
- People lack clear insight into disease risk by location/time
- Applications: travel decisions, awareness
- Keep concise and realistic

2. What Fluence Is
- System that aggregates disease data and provides insights
- Risk estimation / scoring
- Location-based + time-based filtering

3. System Architecture (High-Level)
- Frontend: React/Vite
- Backend: Flask/Python
- Database: Supabase
- External APIs: disease data
- Focus on flow, not deep implementation

4. Key Features (Pick 3–5)
- Heatmap / visualization
- Filtering (location, time, disease)
- API endpoints (structured data)
- Role-based access (if stable)
- Caching / performance improvements

5. AI Component (Keep Vague)
- AI pipeline processes disease data → outputs risk metric
- Mention:
  - preprocessing / normalization
  - dataset construction
  - integration into system
- Avoid deep model specifics unless confident

6. Backend + Data Handling (Optional)
- API routes
- caching layer
- Supabase integration
- Focus on reliability and consistency

7. Demo Plan

Basic flow:
1. Open app
2. Select filters (location/date/disease)
3. Show live updates
4. Highlight risk output / visualization
5. Optional: show fallback or robustness

Keep demo:
- simple
- reliable
- short

8. Challenges
- API integration issues
- async frontend/backend syncing
- data consistency
- local environment setup
- AI pipeline integration

9. Future Work
- improved AI models
- more datasets
- real-time data
- scalability
- UI / mobile improvements

